   Monitoring, documenting and optimizing wastewater plant process controls to
       include adjusting wastewater ﬂow rates, chemical dosage set points, air
       compressor discharge pressures, and blower output settings;
      Maintaining compliance with the Virginia Dept. of Environmental Quality VPDES
       permit and the EPA’s federal regulations;
      Recognizing and correcting negative impacts to wastewater quality;
      Sampling, collecting, documenting chain of custody information, transporting, and
       performing lab testing and analysis on wastewater, sludge, and biosolids samples;
      Monitoring and operating plant equipment and control panels;
      Perform regular preventative maintenance on plant equipment and town facilities;
      General maintenance, housekeeping and grounds as needed.

   Knowledge of wastewater treatment processes;
      Knowledge of general safety practices;
      Ability to safely use hand tools;
      Basic computer knowledge
      Minimum of Class 3 Virginia Wastewater Works Operator License;
      At least 1 year experience in wastewater treatment plant operations;
      Experience with utility plant maintenance;
      Basic general maintenance knowledge

   High School Diploma or GED;
      Virginia’s Driver’s License;
      Desire & Ability to learn new systems, work independently if needed;
      Must be able to work nights, weekends and holidays.

   At least 1 year experience in wastewater treatment plant operations;
      Experience with utility plant maintenance;
      Basic general maintenance knowledge
